1    Basic properties
The general theory of iteration of rational maps has been studied intensively in recent years (see [8], [5], [3]). Everything
we will do in Section 1 has been done in [2] for the case where f is a polynomial with distinct (simple) zeros. Here we
will deal with the case that f may have poles and, most importantly, multiple zeros. Following [2], we start by extending
