is a point. It is clear that any exceptional curve is of the form { y = c}, for some constant c ∈ C ∪ {∞}. In order to work with
points at infinity, we will use the coordinate system (u, v) = j(x, y) = (1/x, 1/ y). We define a∞ = deg(q) − deg(p) so that
f (1/t) = t a∞ h(t), where h(t) is holomorphic at t = 0, and h(0) 6= 0. Thus a∞ gives the order of zero or pole of f at ∞.
