(∞, ∞). For all other cases, { y = c} is not exceptional and is mapped to the vertical line {x = c}. If c = ∞, then we have the
following: If a∞ < 0, then P1 × {∞} is not exceptional; if a∞ ≥ 0, then P1 × {∞} is exceptional and maps to (∞, ∞) x, y .



