Example 4.1 (Möbius transformation.). If f (x) is a Möbius transformation, we may assume it is of the form x−β        x−α
                                                                                                                          , and we
introduce an affine change of coordinate in x to make α = 0 and β = 1. Thus f (x) = x/(x − 1). It follows that S f (x, y) = ( y, x y)
is the Fibonacci monomial map. The basin of (0, 0) for S f corresponds to the basin of the unique root of f (x). The other basin of
S f corresponds to the (degenerate) critical point x = ∞ for f .




